<title>UK: European raw cotton markets see scant demand.</title>
<headline>European raw cotton markets see scant demand.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Limited demand in European raw cotton markets was directed to filling inventory gaps typically for shipment either before or right after the coming summer holidays.</p>
<p>Central Asian, Syrian and West African remained most in focus. Little demand was seen for shipments further forward as most traders were so far reluctant to discount new crop offers enough to tempt mills.</p>
</text>
